# ======================================================================
# WELCOME TO SKODE: "I FEEL LOVE" LIVE-CODING MASTERCLASS
# ======================================================================
# This interactive script will teach you how to perform a track live using 
# Skode's sequencer. We will build Donna Summer's legendary 1977 disco 
# anthem step-by-step.
#
# HOW TO USE THIS GUIDE:
# Do not run the whole file at once! Execute blocks of commands section by 
# section to understand how the song gets built and how to control it.
# ======================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 1: INITIALIZE THE ENGINE & SOUNDS
# (Highlight and execute this block to set up the instruments)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Set tempo to 128 BPM with a 16th-note grid (subdivision 16)
M 128 16

# Drop master volume slightly for headroom
V -20

# Set up the 4 Delay Busses for group effects processing
# Delay Bus 1: Rhythmic syncopation for the Moog Bass
DL 1 4 12 4 0 31 10
DD 1 4 2
DF 1 0
DP 1 0
DG 1 0 0

# Delay Bus 2: Dotted-8th ping-pong for the Pad
DL 2 6 6 6 1 2 15
DD 2 8 1
DF 2 0
DP 2 0
DG 2 0 0

# Delay Bus 3: Short metallic 'room' effect for Drums/Snare
DL 3 3 4 3 10 31 7
DD 3 2 0
DF 3 0
DP 3 0
DG 3 0 0

# Delay Bus 4: Lush Vocal Echo (repurposed for Donna Summer lead)
DL 4 1 20 4 1 2 15
DD 4 8 6
DF 4 0
DP 4 0
DG 4 0 0

# Load classic drum machine samples into k-Synth
[sk/drums-kick.ks]  /ks 1 k>d d>r /r100
[sk/drums-chh.ks]   /ks 1 k>d d>r /r101
[sk/drums-ohh.ks]   /ks 1 k>d d>r /r102
[sk/drums-snare.ks] /ks 1 k>d d>r /r103

# Assign drum voices (0 to 3, plus a linked sub-kick)
v 11 vt [SubKick]  w 100 f 220 a 15 t 0.001 0.1 0 0 # Added ADSR, removed from Track 4
# We use G (Link MIDI) and H (Link Velocity) to chain v 11 to v 0. 
# Now any trigger sent to v 0 automatically triggers v 11 too!
v 0 vt [Kick]      w 100 f 440 a 25 G 11 H 11
v 1 vt [ClosedHat] w 101 f 440 a 2   t 0.001 0.1 0 0  r 3 ds 0.2
v 2 vt [OpenHat]   w 102 f 440 a 3.5 t 0.001 0.8 0 0  r 3 ds 0.3
v 3 vt [Snare]     w 103 f 440 a 15 j 2 0 k 500 q 2 r 3 ds 0.6

# The Iconic Moroder Bass (Voices 4, 5, and 13, layered & detuned)
# We set sustain to 0.0 so the notes NEVER hang when you stop the pattern!
# (Note: when sustain is 0, the release parameter is unused, so we set it to 0).
# j 1 1 applies the 'driven' analog low-pass filter character for extra warmth.
# Voice 4 links to 5 and 13 (G 5 13 H 5 13), so triggering v 4 plays all three!
v 4 vt [MoogBassA]
w 15 a 0  t 0.001 0.18 0 0  j 1 1 k 750 q 2.5  N 0   0   g 0.005  r 1 ds 0.3 G 5 13 H 5 13

v 5 vt [MoogBassB]
w 16 a 2  t 0.001 0.35 0 0  j 1 1 k 750 q 2.5  N -12 10  g 0.005  r 1 ds 0.2

v 13 vt [PureSub]
w 0  a 10 t 0.001 0.50 0 0  N -12 0  # A pure, un-filtered sine wave lingering for gut-scrambling punch

# Filter Stabs (Voices 6 and 8, high resonance)
# j 1 2 applies the 'screamer' analog low-pass character so the resonance squelches.
# We set their N to be relative to the bass root (+36 and +43), and link 6 to 8.
v 6 vt [StabA] n 36
w 15 a -2 t 0.008 0.22 0.0 0.25  j 1 2 k 1800 q 1.3 N 36 0 r 1 ds 0.4 G 8 H 8

v 8 vt [StabB] n 43
w 16 a -6 t 0.008 0.22 0.0 0.25  j 1 2 k 1900 q 1.2 N 43 6 r 1 ds 0.4

# Ethereal Pad (Voices 7 and 9, slow attack, full sustain, glissando)
# We set 'g 0.15' so the pad slides gracefully between chords.
# We set 't 0.8 0 1.0 2.0' (full sustain) so it drones until released!
v 12 vt [TremoloLFO] w 0 f 4 a 1 m 1
# Set N relative to bass (+12 and +19), link 7 to 9.
v 7 vt [PadA] n 36
w 15 a 5  t 0.8 0 1.0 2.0  j 1 0 k  650 q 0.7 N 12 0  g 0.15  r 2 ds 0.6  A 12 0.4 0.6 G 9 H 9

v 9 vt [PadB] n 43
w 18 a 3  t 0.8 0 1.0 2.0  j 1 0 k  700 q 0.6 N 19 -5 g 0.15  r 2 ds 0.6  A 12 0.4 0.6

# "Donna" Vocal Lead (Voices 14 and 15)
# A soaring, full-feeling analog lead mimicking Donna Summer's dramatic vocal shifts.
# Assigned to delay track 4 as requested.
v 14 vt [DonnaA] n 72
w 1 a 0 t 0.01 0.1 0.8 0.6  j 1 0 k 2500 q 1.5 N 0 0 g 0.08 r 4 ds 0.6 G 15 H 15

v 15 vt [DonnaB] n 72
w 3 a -2 t 0.01 0.1 0.8 0.6  j 1 0 k 2500 q 1.5 N 0 8 g 0.08 r 4 ds 0.6


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 2: MACROS (Shortcuts for chords and layers)
# (Execute this block to load the macros)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Bass layer trigger (v 4 naturally triggers 5 and 13 via G/H links)
[Bas]  : v 4 n $$0 l 1 ;

# Root Pitch & Chord updaters (Limited to 4 chars)
# This macro seamlessly transposes the ENTIRE bass pattern on the fly (N 3, N 5, etc.)
# while simultaneously setting the precise target root note for the Pads and Stabs!
[CrdC]  : v 4 N 0 v 5 N -12 v 13 N -12 v 6 n 36 v 7 n 36 ;
[CrdE] : v 4 N 3 v 5 N -9  v 13 N -9  v 6 n 39 v 7 n 39 ;
[CrdF]  : v 4 N 5 v 5 N -7  v 13 N -7  v 6 n 41 v 7 n 41 ;
[CrdG]  : v 4 N 7 v 5 N -5  v 13 N -5  v 6 n 43 v 7 n 43 ;


# Pad chords (Just trigger v 7, it forwards velocity to v 9 via H link!)
[PadC] : v 7 l 1 ;
[PadO] : v 7 l 0 ;       # <--- The crucial note-off for our droning pad!

# Stab chords (Just trigger v 6, it forwards velocity to v 8 via H link!)
[StbC] : v 6 l 1 ;
# Vocal lead triggers
[Voc]  : v 14 n $$0 l 1 ;  # Attack (new breath)
[Vo_]  : v 14 n $$0 ;      # Legato slur (changes pitch without re-triggering envelope!)
[VocO] : v 14 l 0 ;      # Release


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 3: PATTERNS
# (Execute this block to load the musical sequences into memory)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# # Pattern 0: The "Bar Clock". This silent pattern loops every 16 steps 
# (one measure). When we use `zq` to queue pattern changes, Skode waits 
# for this pattern to hit Step 0, keeping everything in perfect sync.
y 0 yt [BarClock]
% 1
[#] x 15

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 4: ORCHESTRATION (The Arrangement)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pattern 1 is our "Master Clock" Orchestrator. We set it to run at a
# 16th of the speed (% 16) so each step equals exactly one full measure.
# We then use immediate-start (/z) commands to trigger our sequences!
# Note: In Skode, a master pattern MUST be a lower number than the 
# patterns it triggers to ensure perfect downbeat alignment.
y 1 yt [Song]
% 16
[ /z 2 1 CrdC ] x 0                    # Start: Drums + Set C Minor
[ /z 3 1 ] x 4                         # Bar 5: Enter Bass
[ /z 7 1 /z 8 1 StbC PadC ] x 8        # Bar 9: Enter Stabs + Pad
[ CrdE ] x 12                         # Bar 13: Bass/Pad/Stabs → Eb
[ /z 7 0 ] x 16                        # Bar 17: Stabs drop out
[ CrdF /z 7 1 /z 9 1 StbC Voc 67 ] x 20 # Bar 21: Bass → F, Stabs return, Vocal Enters
[ /z 9 0 /z 10 1 Voc 67 ] x 24         # Bar 25: Vocal shifts to Climax Pattern
[ CrdG /z 10 0 /z 9 1 Voc 67 ] x 26    # Bar 27: Bass → G, Vocal back to main melody
[ /z 9 0 /z 10 1 Voc 67 ] x 30         # Bar 31: Final hair-lifting vocal climax!
[ CrdC /z 10 0 VocO ] x 32             # Bar 33: Bass → C, Vocal stops
[ /z 3 0 /z 7 0 /z 8 0 PadO ] x 38     # Bar 39: Drop all synths (release Pad)
[ /z 2 0 ] x 44                        # Bar 45: Stop drums, kill any tails
[ /z 1 0 ] x 46                        # Bar 47: Stop song


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 5: INSTRUMENTS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Pattern 2: Four-on-the-floor Drums
y 2 yt [Drums]
% 1
[v 0 l 1]           x 0   # Beat 1: Kick
[v 1 l 1]           x 1   #         Closed Hat
[v 2 l 1]           x 2   #         Open Hat
[v 1 l 1]           x 3   #         Closed Hat

[v 0 l 1  v 3 l 1]  x 4   # Beat 2: Kick + Snare
[v 1 l 1]           x 5   #         Closed Hat
[v 2 l 1]           x 6   #         Open Hat
[v 1 l 1]           x 7   #         Closed Hat

[v 0 l 1]           x 8   # Beat 3: Kick
[v 1 l 1]           x 9   #         Closed Hat
[v 2 l 1]           x 10  #         Open Hat
[v 1 l 1]           x 11  #         Closed Hat

[v 0 l 1  v 3 l 1]  x 12  # Beat 4: Kick + Snare
[v 1 l 1]           x 13  #         Closed Hat
[v 2 l 1]           x 14  #         Open Hat
[v 1 l 1]           x 15  #         Closed Hat

# Pattern 3: The hypnotic 16th-note bassline!
# We no longer need separate patterns for different keys. The Orchestrator
# (or your live macros) simply sends CrdE, CrdF, etc., which transposes
# this exact pattern on the fly via MIDI transposition (N).
y 3 yt [Bass]
% 1
[Bas 36] x 0  [Bas 36] x 2  [Bas 43] x 4  [Bas 46] x 6
[Bas 36] x 8  [Bas 36] x 10 [Bas 43] x 12 [Bas 46] x 14
[#] x 15

y 7 yt [Stabs]
% 1
[StbC] x 0
[StbC] x 8
[#] x 15

# Pattern 8: Sustained Droning Pads
# We make this a 16-bar loop so it only triggers its attack once!
# The Bass pattern forwards the pitch to it, and it glides smoothly.
y 8 yt [Pad]
% 16
[PadC] x 0
[#] x 15

# The "I feel love" 2-bar phrase. Using 8th notes (% 2).
# Notice the use of Vo_ instead of Voc: this creates a true Legato slur 
# where the envelope doesn't restart, seamlessly bending the pitch just like a human singer!
y 9 yt [VocMel]
% 2
# Bar 1: I (beat 1) ... fee-(2.0)-eel(2.5) ... lo-(3.0)-o-(3.5)-ove(4.0) (True Legato Melisma!)
[Voc 67] x 0   [Voc 70] x 2   [Vo_ 72] x 3   [Voc 75] x 4   [Vo_ 74] x 5   [Vo_ 72] x 6   [VocO] x 7
# Bar 2
[Voc 67] x 8   [Voc 70] x 10  [Vo_ 72] x 11  [Voc 75] x 12  [Vo_ 74] x 13  [Vo_ 72] x 14  [VocO] x 15

# The dramatic, soaring climax 2-bar phrase
y 10 yt [VocClm]
% 2
# Bar 1
[Voc 67] x 0   [Voc 70] x 2   [Vo_ 72] x 3   [Voc 75] x 4   [Vo_ 74] x 5   [Vo_ 72] x 6   [VocO] x 7
# Bar 2: The climax! High C6 cascade!
[Voc 67] x 8   [Voc 70] x 10  [Vo_ 72] x 11  [Voc 84] x 12  [Vo_ 82] x 13  [Vo_ 79] x 14  [Vo_ 75] x 15

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 6: LIVE PERFORMANCE GUIDE
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Now you are ready to perform! Execute these commands one by one.

# A. Start the Bar Clock (CRITICAL! This ensures `zq` commands sync properly)
# y 0 z 1

# B. Drop in the Drums (Start them immediately)
# y 2 z 1

# C. Drop in the Bass (Start it immediately)
# y 3 z 1

# D. Perform the progression (Change the chords on the fly!)
# Just execute these macros at the start of a measure to transpose the bass 
# and update the pad roots simultaneously:
# CrdE
# CrdF
# CrdG
# CrdC

# F. Queue the Pads and Stabs (They will drop exactly on the downbeat!)
# y 7 zq 1  y 8 zq 1

# G. Kill everything exactly at the end of the measure
# /z 0 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEP 7: THE HANDS-FREE ORCHESTRATOR
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Want the machine to play it for you? We built a master orchestrator in 
# Pattern 1 that triggers `/z` commands automatically. 
# Make sure to run `/z 0 0` to stop your live jam first!

# Play the full arrangement:
# y 1 zq 1  (Use zq to queue it exactly on the downbeat!)

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# APPENDIX: SKRED LIVE-CODER TIPS & TRICKS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. USE 'zq' NOT 'z' FOR LIVE DROPS: 
#    If the clock is running, dropping a pattern with 'z 1' can hit a modulo math 
#    wrap-around bug that evaluates to step -1 (triggering your STOP commands!). 
#    Always use 'zq 1' to queue safely on the downbeat.
#
# 2. THE 4-CHARACTER RULE:
#    Macros (e.g. [CrdE]) are strictly limited to 4 characters internally. 
#    If you name one [CrdEb], it will be silently truncated and fail to run!
#
# 3. MIND YOUR ENVELOPES:
#    If you link a voice via MIDI (G/H) but forget to give it a 't' (ADSR) 
#    envelope, it will drone infinitely the first time it receives velocity.
#
# 4. LEGATO VS STACCATO:
#    To make a synth "sing" a continuous phrase (melisma) across multiple notes,
#    change the pitch (n) WITHOUT sending 'l 1'. Only send 'l 1' on the first 
#    syllable of the breath.
#
# 5. DELAY BUSES ARE RECORDING STEMS:
#    Routing a voice to 'r 4 ds 0.0' bypasses the delay effect, but it STILL 
#    records that voice to multitrack stem 4. Don't share tracks if you need 
#    clean stems later!
